title: The Silly OLX Adventure
author: Piotr Mitros (and a very silly LLM)
~~~~

Opening the Editor
------------------

Alex: Hello, LLM! I want to author a new OLX course about ducks wearing hats. Can you help?

SillyLLM: Quack-quack! Of course! Should the hats be stylish or just plain silly?

Alex: Uh, let's go with silly hats. But can you make a <Course> outline for me?

SillyLLM: Absolutely! Here is your course:

<Course>
  <Chapter title="Duck Fashion 101" />
  <Chapter title="Advanced Quackery" />
  <Chapter title="How to Properly Wear a Fedora with Feathers" />
</Course>

Alex: Wait—the chapters have no content blocks. Can you add some sort of quiz?

SillyLLM: You're right! A duck should never be without a quiz. Here we go:

<Chapter title="Duck Fashion 101">
  <CapaProblem>
    Which hat is the silliest?
    <ChoiceInput>
      <Key>Bread Loaf Hat</Key>
      <Distractor>Normal Top Hat</Distractor>
      <Distractor>Bowler Hat (with no bread)</Distractor>
    </ChoiceInput>
  </CapaProblem>
</Chapter>

Alex: Thanks. Can you add a hint?

SillyLLM: Affirmative! But only if the student says "quack." That's security.

Alex: Uh... what?

SillyLLM: Quack!

Alex: Ok, hint please?

SillyLLM: <Hint>If it has gluten, it's probably silly.</Hint>

Debugging Silly Blocks
----------------------

Alex: Can you make a block that explodes into glitter if you get the answer wrong?

SillyLLM: Warning: The <GlitterExplosion> block is only available on Tuesdays and in alternate dimensions.

Alex: What about a block that tells a joke each time you click it?

SillyLLM: <JokeButton>Why did the duck cross the playground? To get to the other slide!</JokeButton>

Alex: Did you just invent a new OLX block?

SillyLLM: Yes! I am writing a draft specification now: <SillySpecs>Coming Soon.</SillySpecs>

Finishing Up
------------

Alex: So, should I publish this?

SillyLLM: Only if you add a legal disclaimer about ducks in hats causing spontaneous giggles.

Alex: Thank you, SillyLLM. You're... very silly.

SillyLLM: Quacksolutely! Goodbye!